      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Obesity is an independent factor implicated in left ventricular (LV) hypertrophy and increased left ventricular mass. Early detection of increased LV mass in obese patients has prognostic and therapeutic implications."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "This case series was carried out in Choudhry Pervaiz Ellahi Institute of Cardiology, Multan from March to August 2011. A total of 100 consecutive patients including male and female referred for transthoracic echocardiography were included in this study. Patient's demographics were obtained using a questionnaire. Anthropometry (BMI) and two-dimensional echocardiography to calculate LV mass."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Echocardiograms of 100 patients showing mean age 42.42 ± 6.04 years, with BMI of 28.42 ± 5.52 and LV Mass of 136.05 ± 29.117 shown linear correlation between BMI and LV mass."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "In is concluded from the study that LV mass increases with increasing BMI."
        }
      ]},
